From: H5000M build audit
Subject: [PATCH] mtk_eth_soc: guard integrated PPE unwind when mtkhnat owns PPE

The HNAT build disables integrated PPE init/start/stop through the upstream
999-eth-91 guards. Keep the failure unwind consistent: mtk_ppe_deinit() must
not run for a PPE instance that this configuration never initialized.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -7777,7 +7777,9 @@
 		mtk_napi_del(eth);
 		free_netdev(eth->dummy_dev);
 	}
+#if !defined(CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_HNAT) && !defined(CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_HNAT_MODULE)
 	mtk_ppe_deinit(eth);
+#endif
 	mtk_release_all_muxes(eth);
 	mtk_mdio_cleanup(eth);
 err_free_dev:
